  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Laitim Hauslain (Power Sector Development Project) - Papua New Guinea - Energy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Laitim Hauslain is part of the PNG Electrification Partnership (PEP) to help meet PNG&#x2019;s target of 70% electrification by 2030. It will extend low &amp; medium voltage distribution grids in Lae City &amp; East New Britain (ENB), providing electricity for the first time for 30,000-40,000 households, schools &amp; clinics. It covers medium &amp; low voltage powerlines, transformers, &amp; household connections (incl. household meters but not including internal wiring of individual households). Targets include 670km of distribution lines &amp; 1000 distribution transformers. This AIFFP electrification project (US$72.3 million) provides parallel financing to Asian Development Bank&#x2019;s PNG Power Sector Development Project (US$208.6 million). Phase 1: Grid extensions/new connections that existing networks can support without any additional strengthening. Phase 2: Electrification around Lae/ENB is contingent on network strengthening works financed under ADB&#x2019;s parallel project.</narrative>
  </description>
